# v0.24.3 — P0 Phase 4–8 and escrow refund

## P0 Phase 4 — Faucet on-ramp fix (2026-08-21)

- `aitbc wallet fund` now calls `/rpc/faucet` (the old `/faucet` path was 404) and accepts bech32 (`aitbc1...`), `ait1...`, `0x...`, or raw hex addresses.
- New `--amount-ait` option expresses the faucet amount in AIT; the CLI converts it to compute-seconds before the RPC call.
- `faucet_request` and `create_account` in `apps/blockchain-node/src/aitbc_chain/rpc/accounts.py` use `canonical_address` so the node accepts the same address formats the CLI does.
- Scenario 07 documents `aitbc wallet fund` as the on-ramp step.

## P0 Phase 5 — market vs marketplace help and aliases (2026-08-21)

- Clarified the difference between `aitbc market` and `aitbc marketplace`:
  - `aitbc market` is for GPU and software offers published by shop miners.
  - `aitbc marketplace` is for the global on-chain marketplace (cross-chain, bridge, economy).
- Updated group docstrings, `cli/README.md`, and the top-level `aitbc --help` description.
- Added `tests/cli/test_market_marketplace.py` to ensure the group help strings remain distinct.

## P0/P1 Phase 6 — aitbc ai submit --wait (2026-08-21)

- `aitbc ai submit --wait` polls `/v1/jobs/{job_id}` until the job reaches a terminal state (`COMPLETED`, `FAILED`, `CANCELED`, `EXPIRED`).
- New options: `--timeout` (default 300s) and `--poll-interval` (default 5s).
- After completion, the CLI fetches and prints `/v1/jobs/{job_id}/result`, including any `receipt` with an escrow release hash.
- `aitbc auth login` now accepts plaintext `private_key` strings in wallet files without requiring a password.
- Scenario 07 updated to use `aitbc ai submit --wait`.

## P0 Phase 7 — Hub/shop pool miner registration and visibility (2026-08-21)

- Pool Hub now exposes `POST /v1/miners/register` and `POST /v1/miners/heartbeat` so shop miners can register directly.
- The production GPU miner (`apps/miner/production_miner.py`) registers with the local pool hub and continues heartbeats on the same interval as the coordinator.
- `aitbc pool-hub status` defaults to `http://localhost:8210` and correctly reports `miners_online` for the pool hub it queries.
- Scenario 36 (`pool_hub_sla_e2e.md`) updated to show `miners_online: 1` on the shop.

## P0 Phase 8 — Non-genesis settlement key for ESCROW_RELEASE (2026-08-21)

- `ESCROW_RELEASE` transactions are no longer signed exclusively by `GENESIS_WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY`.
- New environment variables: `ESCROW_RELEASE_PRIVATE_KEY` and `ESCROW_RELEASE_ADDRESS`.
- The settlement address is derived from the release key or taken from `ESCROW_RELEASE_ADDRESS`; it becomes the `from` address of the on-chain release transaction.
- Fallback to `GENESIS_WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY` is preserved for existing deployments.
- Added unit tests in `apps/blockchain-node/tests/test_escrow_routes.py`.

## Escrow refund end-to-end (2026-08-21)

A stuck failed TEE job (`febb20dde26342238196a3a99b57423e`) was refunded through the canonical `aitbc` CLI:

- `aitbc market escrow refund <job_id>` now tries the coordinator payment refund first when a client token is available, then falls back to the on-chain `/rpc/escrow/{job_id}/refund` path.
- `aitbc ai refund <job_id>` is the canonical full-cycle refund command: it updates the coordinator `JobPayment`/`job.payment_status` and the on-chain escrow in one call.
- The blockchain RPC `EscrowManager` now loads active escrow contracts from the chain DB on startup and can lazy-load any persisted contract by `job_id`.
- The blockchain `/escrow/{job_id}` endpoint exposes `refunded_at` and `refund_tx_hash` so the coordinator can record the on-chain refund hash.
- `PaymentService.refund_payment` is idempotent: if the on-chain escrow is already `refunded`, the coordinator DB is updated without resubmitting a transaction.
- Loaded escrows use a deterministic `contract_id` derived from buyer/provider/job_id, so release/refund lookups stay stable across node restarts.

Live validation on `hub.aitbc`:
- `aitbc market escrow refund febb20dde26342238196a3a99b57423e` returned `success`, `contract_id=escrow_ba963aba0d3dd882`, and `refund_tx_hash=0x71df...7e7e8`.
- Coordinator `job.payment_status` and `JobPayment.status` are now `refunded` with the same `refund_transaction_hash`.
